# Agent Memory for Cursor

This repository supports a cross-agent long-term memory vault. Markdown files are the source of truth; SQLite and optional Zvec are indexes only.

## When To Use Memory

Use the memory vault before answering or changing code when the task involves an existing project, prior decisions, paths, user preferences, continuing previous work, reports, research, or non-trivial debugging.

Small one-off tasks such as rephrasing a sentence, translating a short phrase, or checking the time can skip memory lookup.

## Read Flow

1. Resolve the vault root from `AGENT_MEMORY_ROOT`, falling back to `CODEX_MEMORY_ROOT`, then to `templates/vault` for template-only usage.
2. Read the vault `AGENTS.md` or equivalent entry file, then `INDEX.md`.
3. Search with the unified script before guessing which Markdown file to open.
4. Read only the most relevant 1-3 Markdown files. Do not load the whole vault by default.

PowerShell examples:

```powershell
$root = if ($env:AGENT_MEMORY_ROOT) { $env:AGENT_MEMORY_ROOT } elseif ($env:CODEX_MEMORY_ROOT) { $env:CODEX_MEMORY_ROOT } else { "templates/vault" }
Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $root "AGENTS.md") -Raw -Encoding UTF8
Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $root "INDEX.md") -Raw -Encoding UTF8
python scripts/agent_memory_search.py "关键词" --limit 5
```

## Write Flow

Cursor may write stable memory when the user asks to remember something or when an important task ends with durable project facts, decisions, workflows, or agent experience.

Before writing, reconcile with existing memory:

```powershell
python scripts/agent_memory_closeout.py --prewrite "准备写入的记忆摘要"
```

Allowed reconciliation actions are `ADD`, `UPDATE`, `NOOP`, `MARK_OUTDATED`, `MERGE_REQUIRED`, and `ASK_USER`. Stop and ask the user before deleting memory, exposing secrets, spending money, changing credentials, or resolving `MERGE_REQUIRED` / `ASK_USER`.

When Cursor writes a new or rewritten memory, set frontmatter `agent_id: cursor`. Keep `user_id`, `app_id`, `project_id`, `track`, `memory_type`, `status`, and `verified_at` accurate.

After writing, run closeout:

```powershell
python scripts/agent_memory_closeout.py --commit
```

`AGENT_MEMORY_AUTO_COMMIT=1` can make a non-dry-run closeout commit by default. `--dry-run` never commits. If closeout reports `MERGE_REQUIRED`, `ASK_USER`, deleted files, or warnings, stop and ask the user instead of forcing a commit.

## Safety

Do not write API keys, tokens, cookies, passwords, private chat transcripts, SQLite databases, vector stores, or model caches into Markdown or the public repository. Real memory belongs in the local vault selected by `AGENT_MEMORY_ROOT`, not inside this template repository.
